+A fully consumed lookup receipt or definite Busy/rate-limit reply can precede
+the relay's deferred observation of normal request cancellation. Such completed
+exchanges permit only an empty or `canceled` relay context, while the original
+client context must remain empty and the complete exact status/body/hash/write
+must match. Unknown outcomes, client cancellation, partial writes, changed
+deadlines and unpaced retries remain failures. This is a pre-execution evidence
+correction, not a broader retry rule.
